// Dogwood port of policies/transfer_to_team.cedar. transfer_to_team requires a
// non-empty reason, same rule as escalate.dw. Also requires case_id non-empty, for the
// same reason escalate.dw gives: Policy is the independent check, not a rubber stamp
// on what lambdas/tools/schema.json already marks required. Whitespace-only reasons
// ("   ") pass this and are caught by outbound_ivr.tools.business.transfer_to_team in the
// Lambda, same as escalate's own check.
//
// The "at most once per session" half of this tool's rule
// (src/outbound_ivr/voice/agent.py's `state.transfer_to_team_requested` guard) is a separate
// Dogwood temporal policy, policies/dogwood/transfer_to_team_once.dw -- a `forbid` on
// the second-and-later attempt, which composes with this `permit` because forbid
// always overrides permit within a policy engine regardless of which file either rule
// lives in (see "Temporal policies", https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/
// latest/devguide/policy-temporal.html: "You write permit and forbid rules... A
// request is allowed only when a permit applies and no forbid overrides it").
permit(
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"OutboundIvrTools___transfer_to_team",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"${GATEWAY_ARN}"
) when {
  context.input has reason &&
  context.input.reason != "" &&
  context.input has case_id &&
  context.input.case_id != ""
};
